 serif; font-size: 1.1em; color: #8b1e0b;">Ideals:</strong> Freedom. The wilderness belongs to no one. I trust nature more than rulers.<br><strong style="font-family: 'Cinzel', serif; font-size: 1.1em; color: #8b1e0b;">Bonds:</strong> I had a vision of a great draconic spirit; I search for its meaning.<br><strong style="font-family: 'Cinzel', serif; font-size: 1.1em; color: #8b1e0b;">Flaws:</strong> Keeps careful notes of strange sightings and omens<br></p><hr style="border: 0; height: 1px; background: #e0d6c8; margin: 15px 0;"><details style="background: transparent; border: none; box-shadow: none; padding: 0; margin: 0;"><summary style="cursor: pointer; font-weight: bold; color: #8b1e0b; font-size: 1.1em; list-style: none; outline: none; padding: 0; font-family: 'Cinzel', serif;">▶ Read Full Backstory</summary><p style="margin: 15px 0 0 0; font-size: 0.95em; line-height: 1.6; color: #2b2b2b;"> Aros was raised among the deep forests, taught to listen more than he spoke and to observe before acting. From a young age, he felt a connection to something vast and ancient, though he could never name it. One night, while meditating beneath the open sky, Aros experienced a vision of a great draconic spirit soaring above the wilds. The presence did not speak, yet its meaning was clear: the bond between dragon and guardian was not lost to the world. Since then, Aros has wandered beyond his homeland, following instinct and signs only he seems to notice. He believes that when the time is right, the meaning of his vision will be revealed and with it, his true purpose. </p></details></div></div>